"description_full":"CBIZ, Inc. provides financial, insurance, and advisory services in the United States and Canada. It operates through Financial Services, Benefits and Insurance Services, and National Practices segments. The Financial Services segment offers accounting and tax, financial advisory, national technology, and government healthcare consulting services. The Benefits and Insurance Services segment provides employee benefits consulting, payroll/human capital management, property and casualty insurance, and retirement and investment services. The National Practices segment offers information technology managed networking and hardware services. The company primarily serves small and medium-sized businesses, as well as individuals, governmental entities, and not-for-profit enterprises. CBIZ, Inc. was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Independence, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerome P. Grisko Jr. | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $290K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $18K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["CBIZ, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.0B market cap on $2.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 13% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $176M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 53% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8773921850844915},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): durably derated by the market; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Head to Head Survey: Resources Connection (NASDAQ:RGP) and CBIZ (NYSE:CBZ)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/head-to-head-survey-resources-connection-nasdaqrgp-and-cbiz-nysecbz.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794489319.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Comparison: ICF International (NASDAQ:ICFI) & CBIZ (NYSE:CBZ)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/critical-comparison-icf-international-nasdaqicfi-cbiz-nysecbz.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793963706.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here is Why Growth Investors Should Buy CBIZ (CBZ) Now","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022107/here-is-why-growth-investors-should-buy-cbiz-cbz-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_11_growth-3022107","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793724302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CBIZ (NYSE:CBZ) vs. XBP Global (NASDAQ:XBP) Head-To-Head Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/cbiz-nysecbz-vs-xbp-global-nasdaqxbp-head-to-head-survey.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793706304.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Does CBIZ (CBZ) Delisting Mean After Its Take Private Deal Closed?","source":"simplywal